    "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"inputs\": [\n    \"internalTime\",\n    \"TAmb\",\n    \"TDif\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"outputs[1]\",\n    \"outputs[2]\",\n    \"heatCapacitor.T\",\n    \"onOffController.reference\",\n    \"heatingResistor.heatPort.Q_flow\"\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"This scenario probes the behavior of the ControlledTemperature FMU under a combination of step, ramp, and sine excitations. The inputs, such as 'internalTime', 'TAmb', and 'TDif', are used to simulate changes in the ambient conditions and internal temperature over time. A step function will simulate a sudden change in 'TAmb', a ramp function will be applied to 'TDif' to mimic a gradual variation, and a sine wave will be used for 'internalTime' to observe periodic behavior. The outputs, including 'outputs[1]' for the input value, 'outputs[2]' for temperature input, and others related to capacitor temperature, controller reference, and heating flow, will track how the system responds to these variations.\"\n}\n```"
